lization.glm-5.3.findings.md\n?? collab/architect-observe-generalization.glm-5.3.stdout.log\n?? collab/architect-observe-generalization.prompt.md\n?? collab/architect-shared-observation-core-r9.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/architect-shared-observation-core-r9.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/architect-shared-observation-core-r9.prompt.md\n?? collab/architect-space-index-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/architect-space-index-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/architect-space-index-v2-plan.prompt.md\n?? collab/architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.prompt.md\n?? collab/architect-space-transactor-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/architect-space-transactor-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/architect-space-transactor-v2-plan.prompt.md\n?? collab/architect-traces-not-policy.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/architect-traces-not-policy.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/architect-traces-not-policy.prompt.md\n?? collab/architect-v2-consumers.pro.findings.md\n?? collab/architect-v2-consumers.pro.stdout.log\n?? collab/architect-v2-consumers.prompt.md\n?? collab/commit.msg\n?? collab/review-v2-consumers.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md\n?? collab/review-v2-consumers.gpt-5.6-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/review-v2-consumers.prompt.md\n?? collab/stream-v2-rpc-allocator-defect.findings.md\n?? collab/stream-v2-unanswered-request-liveness.findings.md\n?? collab/vm-runtime-semantic-v2.glm-5.3.stdout.log\n?? collab/vm-runtime-semantic-v2.prompt.md\n?? docs/design/dao.space.transactor.md\n docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md                        |  34 +-\n .../adr/0003-dao-space-is-the-event-medium.md      |  26 ++\n docs/design/dao.space.index.md                     |  82 ++--\n docs/design/dao.space.md                           |  67 ++-\n docs/design/dao.space.schema.md                    |  22 +-\n docs/design/dao.stream.md                          |   5 +-\n src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc                      |  68 +--\n src/cljc/dao/space/schema.cljc                     |  56 ++-\n src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc                 | 285 ++++++------\n test/dao/space/index_test.cljc                     |  78 ++--\n test/dao/space/query_test.cljc                     |  11 +-\n test/dao/space/schema_test.cljc                    | 128 +++++-\n test/dao/space/stigmergy_test.clj                  |  36 +-\n test/dao/space/transactor_test.cljc                | 510 ++++++++++-----------\n 14 files changed, 866 insertions(+), 542 deletions(-)\n   489\t## 4. Phase 2 — the swap\n   490\t\n   491\tOne phase: the `defopen` and `DaoStreamLog` cannot be half-deleted, and every\n   492\tconsumer breaks at the same instant.\n   493\t\n   494\t### 4.1 `src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc`\n   495\t\n   496\tDelete `DaoStreamLog`, `ds/defopen :transactor`, the `[dao.stream :as ds]`\n   497\trequire and the `#?(:cljs (:require-macros [dao.stream]))`.\n   498\t\n   499\t- `create!` per D2: validate the spec (reject `:next-t`; require a\n   500\t  `stream/reader?`-and-`stream/writer?` local stream; require a non-empty pool\n   501\t  of `stream/writer?` members — the check at :199-204 is already v2 and moves\n   502\t  verbatim), then `(derive-next-t (index/snapshot-datoms local-stream))` and\n   503\t  return `{:dao.space/transactor true :local-stream … :intake-pool … :name …\n   504\t  :next-t (atom t) :state (atom {:closed false})}`. **No retention check.**\n   505\t- `append-packet!` per D3: `stream/append!`, `stream/valid-outcome?`, advance\n   506\t  on `:dao.stream/ok` only, return the local outcome as data otherwise.\n   507\t- `append!` / `transact!` become plain functions over the value, keeping\n   508\t  `with-write-lock`, `val->datoms`, `entity->datoms`, `pad-datom` and\n   509\t  `derive-next-t` exactly as they are. The closed check returns\n   510\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` instead of throwing.\n   511\t- `close!` sets `:closed` inside the write lock and returns\n   512\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}`; idempotent.\n   513\t- `publish!` reads `(:local-stream log)` / `(:intake-pool log)`.\n   514\t- No `next`, no `closed?`.\n   515\t\n   516\t### 4.2 `src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc`\n   517\t\n   518\t`snapshot-datoms` becomes the v2 read of D6 in full: `checked` on the mint,\n   519\t`checked` on every read, incremental `element-datoms`, three interpreted\n   520\toutcomes, one totality throw, no gap branch. It uses `stream/cursor`,\n   521\t`stream/next` and `stream/validate-outcome` directly; **no `observe` require**.\n   522\t`publish-index!`'s signature is unchanged. The `ds` require survives this phase\n   523\tfor the published adapter only, and dies in Phase 3.\n   524\t\n   525\t### 4.3 `src/cljc/dao/space/schema.cljc`\n   526\t\n   527\tThe seven forced edits in D8's table, under D10's rule. Explicitly untouched:\n   528\t`ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/current` and its opener, `ds/strict-vec` at\n   529\t:260, `ds/realization?` at :259/:318, and `schema_test:304`'s v1 realization\n   530\tfixture. Because D10 re-wraps, **no `schema_test` assertion on a successful\n   531\t`transact!` changes** — which is how three lanes stay green when Phase 2 lands.\n   532\t\n   533\t### 4.4 Tests — the closed inventory\n   534\t\n   535\t`transactor_test` constructs representing local handles, all of which fail the\n   536\tnew v2 surface validation if left on v1:\n   537\t\n   538\t| construct | line | becomes |\n   539\t|---|---|---|\n   540\t| `ReaderOnlyStream` | :25 | v2 reader only — still a negative fixture for `create!`'s surface check |\n   541\t| `WriterOnlyStream` | :33 | v2 writer only — same |\n   542\t| `RecordingAppendStream` | :41 | v2 reader+writer wrapping a `memory-log`, recording appends |\n   543\t| `FailingAppendStream` | :62 | v2 writer answering `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}` then delegating |\n   544\t| `ThrowingAppendStream` | :86 | v2 writer that throws once, then delegates |\n   545\t| concurrency `slow-local` reify | :401 | v2 reader+writer over a `memory-log`, `Thread/sleep` retained |\n   546\t| close-linearization reify | :617 | v2 reader+writer over a `memory-log`, promises retained |\n   547\t\n   548\tIn `index_test`, `MalformedResultStream` (:25) migrates to a **v2 reader**, and\n   549\tis the one double whose migration is not mechanical: v2's `IDaoStreamReader`\n   550\thas both `cursor` and `next`, so it must answer a *conforming* `ok` cursor\n   551\tresult and then return its configured result from every `next`.\n   552\t\n   553\t**`stigmergy_test.clj` — the file r4 cited as end-to-end proof and gave no edit\n   554\tset (F2).** Its four sites, and r4's misstatement corrected: **:106 is the\n   555\ttransactor open, not the agent local**.\n   556\t\n   557\t| site | today | becomes | phase |\n   558\t|---|---|---|---|\n   559\t| :103 | `ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer}` — the agent local | `memory-log/create!` | 2 |\n   560\t| :106 | `ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor …}` | `transactor/create!` | 2 |\n   561\t| :118 | `(count (ds/->seq nil (:local agent)))` — entity-id allocation | the v2 `stream-values` count over the local handle | 2 |\n   562\t| :176-178 | `sources`: `(ds/open! source)` / `ds/strict-vec` / `ds/close!` on an `index/published-index` coordinate | `query/open-published!` → `query/rows` (:495) → `query/close-published!`, keeping `current-state-seq` over the rows | **3** |\n   563\t\n   564\t`:176-178` is the **eleventh** published-adapter read path and the reason this\n   565\tfile is not merely incidental: **every scenario in it calls `sources`**, so\n   566\tPhase 3 breaks the whole file if this is missed.\n   567\t\n   568\tExhaustively, elsewhere: every `ds/append!`, `ds/close!`, `ds/closed?` and\n   569\t`ds/next` whose target is the transactor value becomes the corresponding\n   570\t`transactor/` function; `readers-observe-atomic-transaction-records` (:382)\n   571\tand the read assertion at :609 read `local` rather than `log` (T12); `tx-ts`\n   572\tand every `ds/->seq`/`ds/strict-vec` local-stream helper become one\n   573\t`stream-values` loop, generalizing the existing `intake-values` (:126); all 22\n   574\t`{:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer}` local opens in `transactor_test` become\n   575\t`memory-log/create!`; `descriptor-validation` becomes `spec-validation`; the\n   576\tnamespace docstring's `ds/append!` prose is rewritten. `schema_test:658`'s\n   577\tlocal, `index_test`'s `open-local` (:68) and `query_test`'s `open-local`\n   578\t(:567) all become `memory-log/create!`.\n   579\t\n   580\t**The residue greps are the closure criterion**, not the lists —\n   581\t`grep -c \"ds/\"`:\n   582\t\n   583\t| file | today | after |\n   584\t|---|---|---|\n   585\t| `transactor_test.cljc` | 135 | 0 (Phase 2) |\n   586\t| `query_test.cljc` | 2 | 0 (Phase 2) |\n   587\t| `index_test.cljc` | 41 | 0 (Phase 3) |\n   588\t| `stigmergy_test.clj` | 6 | 3 after Phase 2, **0** after Phase 3 |\n   589\t\n   590\t### 4.5 The ring-buffer site accounting\n   591\t\n   592\t- **28** unbounded `ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer}` sites.\n   593\t  `query_test:97` is a literal map passed to `q` to prove a raw map is rejected\n   594\t  as a db input — not an open, and unchanged.\n   595\t- `schema_test:304` stays v1: a closed v1 realization for `schema/current`'s\n   596\t  borrowed-input path, which is schema's own surface.\n   597\t- The other **27 migrate**, including `index_test:777`'s descriptor carrier —\n   598\t  the one migrated site that becomes a **v2 ring buffer** rather than a\n   599\t  memory-log, because the point of that test is that a coordinate is ordinary\n   600\t  data on an ordinary stream and nothing about a carrier needs complete\n   601\t  retention.\n   602\t- `index_test:379`'s capacity-bearing gap fixture is **deleted** with S5 (§7).\n   603\t- Every other migrated site is a `dao.space` local stream and becomes\n   604\t  `memory-log/create!`. There is no capacity to choose: the transport declares\n   605\t  no capacity key, and passing `:dao.stream.memory-log/capacity` is\n   606\t  `invalid-spec` by construction.\n   607\t\n   608\t### 4.6 Proof\n   609\t\n   610\tUnchanged deftests carry most of it: `reopen-derives-next-t-from-retained-\n   611\thistory` (:291) for T2, the three malformed sub-cases of\n   612\t`malformed-or-gapped-retained-history-throws` (:336, :344, :352) for T4a,\n   613\t`each-transaction-is-exactly-one-append` (:366) for T1,\n   614\t`append-failure-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry` (:499) and\n   615\t`append-throw-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry` (:515) for T5 — the first now\n   616\tobserving a returned outcome instead of a catch —\n   617\t`close-is-per-handle-and-does-not-touch-local-stream` (:584) for T7,\n   618\t`close-linearizes-after-an-in-flight-append` (:616) for T8,\n   619\t`single-writer-wrappers-are-not-coordinated` (:655) for T6,\n   620\t`publish-enqueues-indexes-into-the-pool` (:681) for T11.\n   621\t\n   622\tFive new tests:\n   623\t\n   624\t1. **T14's replacement** — `append!` and `transact!` after `close!` each answer\n   625\t   `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` rather than throwing.\n   626\t2. **S6 and S10, on `MalformedResultStream`.** Its two existing sub-cases stay\n   627\t   (a map without `:cursor`; an unknown signal), plus **two new ones**:\n   628\t   - a repeated `ok` carrying `:dao.stream/value` but no `:dao.stream/cursor`\n   629\t     must terminate by **throwing**, not spin (r4/P1-1);\n   630\t   - a **conforming** `gap` — outcome plus its required `:dao.stream/cursor` —\n   631\t     must hit the totality throw (F4). This is the only pin on S10 once §7\n   632\t     deletes the gap test, and it is legitimate where a transport fixture is\n   633\t     not: `conformance.cljc` forbids a *fixture inducing an excluded outcome\n   634\t     on the transport*, not a double proving the consumer's own precondition\n   635\t     check. Pair it with a `cursor-mismatch` case for the same reason.\n   636\t3. **T19 and T20, in `schema_test`** — a `memory-log`-backed writer double\n   637\t   answering `full` once then succeeding. Assert: after the failed\n   638\t   `schema/transact!` the wrapper's schema and uniqueness state are identical\n   639\t   to before; the returned value is the conforming non-ok outcome; the retry\n   640\t   commits at the **same** `t`; and on success the receipt is still\n   641\t   `{:result :ok :t … :datoms …}` (D10). The only way to exercise D3's non-ok\n   642\t   path, since the real transport excludes `full`.\n   643\t4. **T8's lock extension** — `schema/publish!` while a close is in flight\n   644\t   resolves one way or the other, never publishing after the close returned.\n   645\t   JVM-only, alongside the existing linearization test.\n   646\t5. **T15 on the transactor itself** — the v2 receipt shape, asserted where the\n   647\t   14 existing `{:result :ok …}` assertions in `transactor_test` are migrated.\n   648\t   Note the deliberate asymmetry with #3: the transactor's public result\n   649\t   migrates because the transactor is being migrated; schema's does not\n   650\t   because schema is not (D10).\n   651\t\n   652\t### 4.7 Docs, in-phase\n   653\t\n   654\t- `docs/design/dao.space.index.md` — replace the `ds/open! {:dao.stream/type\n   655\t  :transactor …}` sample (:195-210) and the descriptor sentence (:191) with\n   656\t  `memory-log/create!` + `transactor/create!`; restate *The snapshot* on the\n   657\t  transport's declared retention (S1, S8, S9, S10); delete the\n   658\t  gap-aborts-publication sentence (S5); carry §8's placement.\n   659\t- `docs/design/dao.space.md` — *The Write Path* sample at :509, the descriptor\n   660\t  mention at :476, §8's placement, and **:390's \"The local stream is the\n   661\t  durable record\"**. Per D4 that sentence contradicts the two stages printed\n   662\t  around it; it becomes: the local stream is authoritative for its process\n   663\t  lifetime, **the durable record is what publication puts in `dao.jing`**, and\n   664\t  un-published writes are not durable — which the paragraph's own\n   665\t  memory-index → disk-index analogy already implies. Add that a durable\n   666\t  *stream* transport is not the fix, with the pointer to\n   667\t  `dao.space.query.md`'s ruled-out `dao.stream`/`dao.jing` unification.\n   668\t- `docs/design/dao.space.schema.md` — :383's \"opens the inner `:transactor`\"\n   669\t  becomes a transactor *value*; the wrapper owns its own closedness; and D10's\n   670\t  rule is recorded so schema's own plan knows what it inherits.\n   671\t- `docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md` — step 1's \"each agent owns a local\n   672\t  `dao.stream`\" becomes a `memory-log`; step 2's `ds/append!`/`:transactor`\n   673\t  becomes `transactor/create!` and `transactor/append!`/`transact!`; and :38's\n   674\t  \"durable\" claim is corrected per D4.\n   675\t- `docs/design/adr/0003-dao-space-is-the-event-medium.md` — an **amendment\n   676\t  note**, not a supersession. The decision is untouched; two *Consequences*\n   677\t  bullets go stale: `DaoStreamLog` no longer exists and the deposit target is\n   678\t  `transactor/append!`, a plain function on a value; and the retention bullet's\n   679\t  \"`:dao.stream/full`, `:dao.stream/gap` so loss is never silent\" needs §8's\n   680\t  pointer — the local log excludes both, and its completeness comes from the\n   681\t  declaration.\n   682\t- `docs/design/dao.stream.md` — drop `transactor` from the remaining-consumer\n   683\t  list; `index` goes in Phase 3.\n   684\t- **A new permanent `dao.space.transactor` section** (or its own doc, owner's\n   685\t  call) carrying T1–T11, T15, T16, T18, T19, T20, D3's outcome table, §8's\n   686\t  placement, and D4's O(history) note as an Open item. It must state where\n   687\t  durability lives rather than omitting the subject, and must **not** claim the\n   688\t  local stream is durable.\n   689\t\n   690\t## 5. Phase 3 — index closes\n   691\t\n   692\t### 5.1 What is built\n   693\t\n   694\tOne rewritten `defopen` body in `dao.space.schema`:\n   695\t\n   696\t```clojure\n   697\t(ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/published\n   698\t  [descriptor]\n   699\t  ;; validate exactly as today, then:\n   700\t  (let [store (jing-coordinate/open! content-store)\n   701\t        rows  (try (index/read-datoms store manifest-address)\n   702\t                   (finally (jing/close! store)))]\n   703\t    (->PublishedSchemaRows rows)))\n   704\t```\n   705\t\n   706\t`PublishedSchemaRows` is a small private record in `schema.cljc` implementing\n   707\t`ds/IDaoStreamReader` (`next` by position over the vector) and\n   708\t`ds/IDaoStreamBound` (`close!` → `{:woke []}` per D10, `closed?` → true). This\n   709\tis *simpler* than what it replaces: schema forces the whole row vector at open\n   710\tanyway (`ds/strict-vec` at :1167), so nothing on this path needed the lazy\n   711\trestored trees or a retained store handle.\n   712\t\n   713\t### 5.2 What is deleted\n   714\t\n   715\t- `schema.cljc:1161` `ds/open! (index/published-index …)` and `:1167`\n   716\t  `ds/strict-vec`.\n   717\t- `index.cljc:344-363` `PublishedIndexStream`.\n   718\t- `index.cljc:383-404` `ds/defopen :dao.space.index/published`.\n   719\t- `index.cljc`'s `[dao.stream :as ds]` and `[dao.jing.coordinate]` requires.\n   720\t- `index_test`'s and `stigmergy_test`'s `[dao.stream :as ds]` requires.\n   721\t\n   722\t### 5.3 What Phase 3 must not touch\n   723\t\n   724\t`ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/current` (:357) and its opener; `SchemaWrapper`\n   725\t(:943-955) beyond D8's edits; `ds/strict-vec` at :260 and `ds/realization?` at\n   726\t:259/:318; `schema_test:304`'s v1 fixture; schema's closedness model beyond\n   727\tD8's table.\n   728\t\n   729\t### 5.4 The eleven adapter read paths\n   730\t\n   731\tTen call sites across eight deftests in `index_test`, **plus `stigmergy_test`'s\n   732\t`sources` (F2)**. Seven `index_test` deftests leave; one stays. A deleted test\n   733\twhose property is not covered elsewhere is a defect, so each is accounted for:\n   734\t\n   735\t| # | site | property | disposition |\n   736\t|---|---|---|---|\n   737\t| 1 | `open-published-rejects-unresolvable-and-malformed-descriptors` (:586; 600, 611) | unsupported coordinate type fails closed; extra key rejected — P1 | **Moved** onto `query/open-published!` in `query_test`; nothing there covers coordinate rejection today. |\n   738\t| 2 | `open-published-rejects-missing-and-invalid-manifests` (:624; 637, 647) | missing manifest throws; stored non-manifest throws | **Deleted.** Covered by `read-manifest-guards-missing-and-invalid` (:823), on the functions both openers call. |\n   739\t| 3 | `published-realization-is-read-only-with-a-stable-lifecycle` (:651; 656) | P6 and P7; EAVT order | **Deleted.** P6 dies with the adapter; P7 is dropped. EAVT order survives in #7; idempotent close survives as `close-published-closes-once-and-is-idempotent` (`query_test`:715). |\n   740\t| 4 | `published-empty-index-drains-to-end` (:681; 683) | an empty manifest reads as no datoms | **Deleted, with one addition.** `publish-index-of-empty-input-is-readable` (:351) covers it via `read-datoms`; add a `query_test` case that `open-published!` on an empty manifest yields an empty relation. |\n   741\t| 5 | `published-open-fetches-only-the-manifest` (:690; 700) | exactly one fetch at open, zero nodes faulted — P3 | **Moved.** `lazy-published-node-budget-is-strictly-bounded` (:737) bounds *total* gets at ≤ 4; it does not pin the open-time count. Add `open-published-fetches-only-the-manifest` asserting exactly 1 get after open and before any read. |\n   742\t| 6 | `covered-indexes-returns-the-four-covered-sets` (:708; 710, 732) | P8 | **Stays, split.** Its four structural cases need no opened value and no fixture and remain verbatim — the deftest loses its `publish-into-file` fixture entirely. Only the opened-value assertion moves, onto `query/open-published!`'s value; that move is itself P8's proof. |\n   743\t| 7 | `published-next-yields-the-same-eavt-rows-as-the-eager-walk` (:736; 741) | P4 | **Moved.** `open-published!`'s forced `:rows` versus `index/read-datoms`. |\n   744\t| 8 | `published-index-is-a-transportable-bounded-stream` (:759; 783, carrier :777) | P2 | **Moved and modernized.** Keep the `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip and the carrier, now a v2 ring buffer, and open the transported coordinate with `query/open-published!`. Assert the **complete exact coordinate map**; `ds/exact-bound?` (:779) is v1 and is replaced by that equality. |\n   745\t| **9** | **`stigmergy_test.clj:176-178`, `sources`** | the production read path every scenario in the file depends on | **Migrated** to `query/open-published!` → `query/rows` → `query/close-published!`, keeping `current-state-seq` over the rows and the `try`/`finally`. Not a test of the adapter — a *use* of it, which is why missing it would have broken every scenario rather than one assertion. |\n   746\t\n   747\t**Plus one test the adapter never had:** P5 — \"a store opened during a failed\n   748\topen is closed before the error propagates\" — has no covering test anywhere,\n   749\tand the survivors above prove validation errors, not ownership cleanup. Add a\n   750\t`query/open-published!` test with a close-counting store whose manifest read\n   751\tfails after `jing-coordinate/open!` succeeds; assert the original error\n   752\tpropagates and the store is closed **exactly once**.\n   753\t\n   754\t### 5.5 Residue\n   755\t\n   756\t`index_test`: after Phase 2 migrates `open-local` (:68), `stream-values`\n   757\t(:122), `MalformedResultStream` (:25) and the carrier (:777), and Phase 3\n   758\tremoves the seven adapter deftests, strips the fixture and open from the\n   759\teighth, and deletes the gap fixture (:375-392), `grep -c \"ds/\"` returns **0**\n   760\t(currently 41).\n     1\tCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-09 12:21 GMT\n     2\tCompleted-Local: 2026-09-09 19:21 +0700 (Asia/Bangkok)\n     3\tCoding-Agent: glm\n     4\tSession-ID: 6a2bae02-ee7f-47b6-ae80-e905b0ca657f\n     5\t\n     6\t# Phase 2 complete — the swap\n     7\t\n     8\tBranch `dao.stream-redesign-v2` at `e467687` (Phase 1), tree clean before\n     9\tthe edit. Phase 2 of the r5 plan (§4) only, landed as one coherent change:\n    10\tthe tree did not compile between the `transactor.cljc` rewrite and the test\n    11\tmigrations, as the plan promised. 14 files modified + 1 new doc; nothing\n    12\tstaged, nothing committed.\n    13\t\n    14\t## What was done\n    15\t\n    16\t### `src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc` — rewritten (§4.1)\n    17\t\n    18\t- `DaoStreamLog`, `ds/defopen :transactor`, the `[dao.stream :as ds]`\n    19\t  require and the `#?(:cljs (:require-macros [dao.stream]))` are all\n    20\t  deleted. The namespace now requires exactly `dao.datom`,\n    21\t  `dao.space.index`, `dao.stream` — the §6 end condition for this\n    22\t  namespace, verified by grep (all remaining `dao.stream` mentions are\n    23\t  `:dao.stream/…` outcome keywords, `dao.stream`, or prose).\n    24\t- `create!` per D2: rejects `:next-t`; requires a `stream/reader?`-and-\n    25\t  `stream/writer?` local stream; requires a non-empty pool of\n    26\t  `stream/writer?` members (the v2 check moved verbatim, message keeps\n    27\t  `IDaoStreamWriter` since that is the protocol `stream/writer?` gates);\n    28\t  derives `t` via `derive-next-t (index/snapshot-datoms …)`; returns\n    29\t  `{:dao.space/transactor true :local-stream … :intake-pool … :name …\n    30\t  :next-t (atom t) :state (atom {:closed false})}` — the value or a throw.\n    31\t  **No retention check** (T18's declaration lives in docstrings and docs).\n    32\t- `append-packet!` per D3: `stream/append!` → `stream/valid-outcome?` before\n    33\t  any interpretation → advance watermark and answer the v2 receipt\n    34\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.space/t t :dao.space/datoms ds}`\n    35\t  on ok; return the conforming non-ok answer as data with the watermark\n    36\t  unchanged; fold a non-outcome answer to `:dao.stream/transport-error`\n    37\t  with the raw answer under `:dao.stream/answer`.\n    38\t- `append!`/`transact!` are plain functions over the value, keeping\n    39\t  `with-write-lock`, `val->datoms`, `entity->datoms`, `pad-datom` and\n    40\t  `derive-next-t` verbatim. The closed check answers\n    41\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` as data (T14's replacement);\n    42\t  the argument-defect throws (no `:db/id`, explicit `t`, empty `tx-data`,\n    43\t  zero datoms) all survive.\n    44\t- `close!` sets `:closed` under the write lock and answers\n    45\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}`; idempotent. `publish!` reads\n    46\t  `(:local-stream log)`/`(:intake-pool log)`. No `next`, no `closed?`.\n    47\t\n    48\t### `src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc` — snapshot-datoms (§4.2/D6)\n    49\t\n    50\t- Private `checked` added: `stream/validate-outcome` on the mint and on\n    51\t  **every** read, throwing \"malformed local stream result\" carrying\n    52\t  `{:operation :result :defect}` — validate-before-interpret, so a\n    53\t  malformed `ok` with no cursor throws instead of recurring on nil\n    54\t  (r4/P1-1; §4.6 #2's spin case is converted to a throw).\n    55\t- `snapshot-datoms` is D6's loop in full: `stream/cursor … :dao.stream/oldest`\n    56\t  mint (non-ok mint throws \"local stream refused an :oldest cursor\"),\n    57\t  `case` over `ok` (incremental `element-datoms` inside the loop — S8\n    58\t  preserved), `(:dao.stream/blocked :dao.stream/end)` finish at the tail,\n    59\t  one totality throw (\"local stream is not a complete-retention transport\")\n    60\t  for a well-formed unexpected outcome. **No gap branch** (S5 deleted).\n    61\t  No `observe` require. D6's docstring used verbatim.\n    62\t- `publish-index!`'s docstring sentence \"a retention gap throws before\n    63\t  emission\" replaced with the S9 statement (complete-retention transport\n    64\t  required; snapshot completes before emission). `publish-index!`'s\n    65\t  signature and body are otherwise untouched. The `ds` require survives\n    66\t  for the published adapter only (D7: :347/:358/:383 are the remaining\n    67\t  `ds/` sites, all Phase 3's).\n    68\t\n    69\t### `src/cljc/dao/space/schema.cljc` — the seven forced edits (§4.3/D8/D10)\n    70\t\n    71\t1. `:965` `ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor …}` → `tx/create!` over a\n    72\t   plain spec.\n    73\t2. `SchemaWrapper.close!` sets its own `:closed` **and** calls `tx/close!`\n    74\t   under the wrapper lock, returning `{:woke []}` (D10 re-wrap).\n    75\t3. `SchemaWrapper.closed?` reads `(:closed @state)` — the wrapper owns the\n    76\t   flag, since the transactor no longer has `closed?`.\n    77\t4. `transact!` installs `next-state` **only on `:dao.stream/ok`** (T19) and\n    78\t   re-wraps the ok receipt to `{:result :ok :t t :datoms ds}` (D10/T20); a\n    79\t   conforming non-ok outcome is returned unchanged. **No `schema_test`\n    80\t   assertion on a successful `transact!` changed** — the full diff of\n    81\t   schema_test contains zero edits to existing `:result`/`:t`/`:datoms`\n    82\t   assertions, and W38–W41 ran unmodified.\n    83\t5. `publish!`'s closedness guard moved under the wrapper lock, serialized\n    84\t   with `tx/publish!` — the lock is now held across an index build, as the\n    85\t   plan prices in.\n    86\t6. `:926`/`:969` `index/snapshot-datoms` sites unchanged; the handle is now\n    87\t   a memory-log.\n    88\t7. `schema/transactor`'s `local-stream` callers pass memory-log handles\n    89\t   (test-side change, below).\n    90\t\n    91\tExplicitly untouched, verified: `ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/current` and\n    92\tits opener, `ds/strict-vec` at :260, `ds/realization?`, and\n    93\t`schema_test:304`'s v1 realization fixture.\n    94\t\n    95\t### Tests (§4.4)\n    96\t\n    97\t**`transactor_test.cljc`** — every `ds/` gone (135 → 0). The five doubles\n    98\tmigrated (`ReaderOnlyStream`/`WriterOnlyStream` now v1-surface negatives\n    99\tagainst `create!`'s v2 surface check; `RecordingAppendStream`/\n   100\t`FailingAppendStream`/`ThrowingAppendStream` are v2 reader+writer wrappers\n   101\tover a memory-log); the two JVM `reify` doubles (concurrency slow-local,\n   102\tclose-linearization) likewise; all 22 `{:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer}`\n   103\tlocal opens became `memory-log/create!`; `descriptor-validation` became\n   104\t`spec-validation`; `tx-ts` and every `ds/->seq` became one `stream-values`\n   105\tloop; reads in `readers-observe-atomic-transaction-records` go through\n   106\t`local` (T12); the gap sub-case of\n   107\t`malformed-or-gapped-retained-history-throws` deleted (§7), the deftest\n   108\trenamed `malformed-retained-history-throws` with the three malformed\n   109\tsub-cases kept; `append-failure-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry` now\n   110\tobserves the returned `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}` instead of a\n   111\tcatch; `local-still-open?` (blocked-vs-end at the tail) replaces every\n   112\t`ds/closed? local`-class assertion, v2 having no closed? predicate. All 14\n   113\t`{:result :ok …}` receipt assertions migrated to the v2 receipt — T15\n   114\tpinned. T14's replacement is asserted twice (append! and transact! after\n   115\tclose answer `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}`). While migrating\n   116\t`ThrowingAppendStream` I found and fixed a latent v1 bug: its success\n   117\tbranch called `(ds/append! inner val)` with `val` unbound — resolving to\n   118\tthe clojure.core function — so the retry appended `#'clojure.core/val` to\n   119\tthe stream instead of the packet; no v1 assertion observed the stream\n   120\tcontents, so it was invisible. The double now appends the actual value.\n   121\t\n   122\t**`index_test.cljc`** — `MalformedResultStream` is a v2 reader (conforming\n   123\t`ok` cursor mint, configured result from every `next`); `open-local` is a\n   124\tmemory-log; `publish-index-gap-local-stream-throws-before-emission` deleted\n   125\t(§7). The malformed-result deftest keeps its two existing sub-cases and\n   126\tadds three: a repeated `ok` carrying `:dao.stream/value` but no\n   127\t`:dao.stream/cursor` (throws \"malformed\", does not spin), a **conforming**\n   128\t`gap` (outcome + required cursor) and a conforming `cursor-mismatch`, both\n   129\thitting the totality throw `#\"complete-retention\"` — S10's only pins now\n   130\tthe gap test is gone (F4). `stream-values` (:122) and the :777 carrier were\n   131\t**not** migrated: their only callers are the published-adapter deftests\n   132\tPhase 3 removes/moves (§5.4 #6–#8), so migrating them this phase would have\n   133\tbroken v1 tests that survive until Phase 3. `index_test`'s `ds/` count is\n   134\ttherefore 35 (41 − open-local ×2 − the double's protocol + its comment −\n   135\tthe gap fixture ×2), on the path to 0 at Phase 3.\n   136\t\n   137\t**`stigmergy_test.clj`** — `:103` the agent local is a memory-log; `:106`\n   138\tthe transactor is `transactor/create!`; `:118` entity-id allocation counts\n   139\tvia a `local-values` v2 loop; the `[dao.stream.ringbuffer]` require removed\n   140\twith the `:103` migration (the adversarial review's lint-only nit). The\n   141\t`[dao.stream :as ds]` require stays — `sources`' three sites (:188-190)\n   142\tare Phase 3's (§5.4 #9). Two comments naming the dead `:transactor` type\n   143\ttidied.\n   144\t\n   145\t**`query_test.cljc`** — `open-local` is a memory-log; the `[dao.stream :as\n   146\tds]`, `[dao.stream.ringbuffer]` requires and the cljs `require-macros`\n   147\tremoved with the last two `ds/` sites (2 → 0).\n   148\t\n   149\t**`schema_test.cljc`** — `fresh-streams`' local is a memory-log (intake\n   150\tstays a v2 ringbuffer); `closed-wrapper-throws`'s `(ds/closed? local)`\n   151\treplaced with the blocked-at-tail observable (v1 `closed?` on a memory-log\n   152\twould throw — no protocol impl); `reified-metadata-reference-seeds-wrapper-state`\n   153\tappends via `stream/append!`. Two new deftests:\n   154\t\n   155\t- `failed-inner-append-leaves-wrapper-state-unchanged` (§4.6 #3, T19/T20) —\n   156\t  a memory-log-backed writer double refusing exactly the second append\n   157\t  (bootstrap passes, first data tx gets `full`, retry passes): the returned\n   158\t  value is the conforming `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}`;\n   159\t  `(wrapper-state w)` is `=` to the pre-failure state; the retry's receipt\n   160\t  is exactly `{:result :ok, :t 1, :datoms [[7 :person/name \"Alice\" 1 1]]}`\n   161\t  — same `t` the refused attempt planned, v1 shape intact (D10); state\n   162\t  advances only on the success.\n   163\t- `publish-serializes-against-close` (§4.6 #4, T8's lock extension,\n   164\t  JVM-only) — a slow-reader double blocks the publication inside its\n   165\t  snapshot under the wrapper lock; `close!` derefs to `::timeout` while the\n   166\t  publication is in flight (it cannot return around it); after release the\n   167\t  in-flight publication completes with the full history, `close!` returns\n   168\t  `{:woke []}`, and a publish started after the close returns throws\n   169\t  `#\"closed\"`.\n   170\t\n   171\t### Docs (§4.7) — all seven\n   172\t\n   173\t- **New `docs/design/dao.space.transactor.md`** (the permanent record;\n   174\t  owner's call was its own doc, following the `dao.space.index.md`\n   175\t  pattern): D1's value framing and sample, the T1–T11/T15/T16/T18–T20\n   176\t  table, D3's outcome table, T18 in full (required transport by name,\n   177\t  detectable-but-deliberately-unchecked with the coupling reason, and the\n   178\t  sentence \"a reader/writer surface check does not establish retention\"),\n   179\t  where durability lives (never claiming the local stream is durable), and\n   180\t  D4's O(history) replay as an Open item with the one-truth checkpoint\n   181\t  direction. Linked from `dao.space.md` and `dao.space.index.md` related\n   182\t  lists.\n   183\t- `dao.space.index.md` — *The snapshot* restated on declared retention\n   184\t  (S1/S8/S9/S10, validate-outcome, totality throw; the gap sentence\n   185\t  deleted); the agent-transactor loop sample is `memory-log/create!` +\n   186\t  `transactor/create!`; §8's placement in both *The snapshot* and the loop\n   187\t  section.\n   188\t- `dao.space.md` — :390's \"The local stream is the durable record\" replaced\n   189\t  by D4's corrected statement (authoritative for process lifetime; the\n   190\t  durable record is what publication puts in dao.jing; a durable stream\n   191\t  transport is not the fix, with the query.md pointer); the :476 descriptor\n   192\t  sentence now names the transactor value; the write-path sample (:509)\n   193\t  fully rewired (memory-log local, v2 intake + observer-state entry,\n   194\t  `transactor/create!`/`append!`); §8's placement beside the sample.\n   195\t- `dao.space.schema.md` — :383 becomes the transactor value + wrapper-owned\n   196\t  closedness + install-only-on-ok; D10's rule recorded as its own\n   197\t  paragraph so schema's own plan knows what it inherits.\n   198\t- `dao.space.stigmergy.md` — step :38's \"durable\" claim corrected per D4;\n   199\t  §2 (the implemented write path) and the minimum-stack step 2 rewired on\n   200\t  memory-log + `transactor/create!`/`append!`/`transact!`.\n   201\t- ADR 0003 — an **amendment note** (2026-09-09), decision untouched:\n   202\t  DaoStreamLog is gone and the deposit target is `transactor/append!`, a\n   203\t  plain function on a value; the writer-face precondition is now met for\n   204\t  operational outcomes (the exception's second trigger remains open, so the\n   205\t  exception stands); the retention bullet gets its §8 pointer (the local\n   206\t  log excludes both `full` and `gap`; completeness comes from the\n   207\t  declaration).\n   208\t- `dao.stream.md` — consumer list drops `transactor`: \"`dao.space` (index\n   209\t  and schema — `query` and `transactor` migrated, …)\".\n   210\t\n   211\t## Verification — exact commands and counts\n   212\t\n   213\t| lane | command | result |\n   214\t|---|---|---|\n   215\t| clj | `bb test:clj` | **Ran 1433 tests containing 165353 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.** (1432/165341 at Phase 1; +1 net deftest: 2 added in schema_test, 1 gap deftest deleted in index_test) |\n   216\t| cljs | `bb test:cljs` | **Ran 1343 tests containing 34920 assertions. 0 failures, 1 errors.** `Testing dao.space.transactor-test`, `…index-test`, `…schema-test` all present and green in the node output (verified by grep) |\n   217\t| cljd | `bb test:cljd` (built `build/slice-peer` + `build/yin-repl-peer`, then `clojure -M:cljd test`) | **All tests passed!** (+1296; +1 vs Phase 1's +1295). All 14 transactor-test deftests and the three new schema deftests enumerated in the run output |\n   218\t| demo | `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo` | **Build completed. (212 files, 12 compiled, 0 warnings, 3.46s)** |\n   219\t| kondo | `clj -M:kondo --lint` on all 8 touched code files | **0 errors, 4 warnings, 5 infos — every one pre-existing.** `index.cljc:347/:360` (PublishedIndexStream, Phase 3 deletes it) and `schema.cljc:947` / `stigmergy_test.clj:71` verified present at HEAD by stdin-linting `git show HEAD:…`. Net improvement: old `transactor.cljc` carried 3 warnings (Missing protocol method: cursor; Unresolved close! ×2-class), the rewrite carries 0; the Phase-1 `index_test.cljc:30` warning is gone with the double's migration |\n   220\t| format | `mise exec -- cljstyle fix <same 8 files>` then `cljstyle check` | fix reformatted 3 test files (alignment only); check exits clean. Both clj and cljs and cljd re-run **after** the reformat — the counts above are post-format |\n   221\t\n   222\tThe one cljs error is the pre-existing `wasm-eval-emits-telemetry-test`\n   223\t(`ReferenceError: wasm is not defined`, `telemetry_test.cljc:101-109`),\n   224\tdocumented in Phase 1's findings as baked into base history (`78b5262`);\n   225\tthis phase does not touch that file. No hang anywhere: the suite runs in\n   226\tits normal time, so the D6 spin regression the plan warned about is\n   227\tconverted to a throw as required (and pinned by the no-cursor sub-case).\n   228\t\n   229\t## Residue greps (the closure criteria)\n   230\t\n   231\t```\n   232\t$ grep -c \"ds/\" test/dao/space/transactor_test.cljc   0   (was 135 → Phase 2 criterion met)\n   233\t$ grep -c \"ds/\" test/dao/space/stigmergy_test.clj     3   (was 6 → Phase 2 criterion met;\n   234\t                                                            remaining = sources :188-190, Phase 3)\n   235\t$ grep -c \"ds/\" test/dao/space/query_test.cljc        0   (was 2)\n   236\t$ grep -c \"ds/\" test/dao/space/index_test.cljc       35   (was 41; 0 is the Phase 3 criterion)\n   237\t```\n   238\t\n   239\tThe three remaining stigmergy sites are exactly `sources`' `ds/open!` /\n   240\t`ds/strict-vec` / `ds/close!` (§5.4 #9). `src` side: `grep -n \"ds/\"\n   241\tsrc/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc` returns exactly D7's three Phase-3 rows\n   242\t(:347, :358, :383); `transactor.cljc` returns nothing (the one grep hit at\n   243\t:48 is the substring in \"appends/transacts\"). `transactor.cljc` requires\n   244\texactly `dao.datom`, `dao.space.index`, `dao.stream`.\n   245\t\n   246\t## Plan invariants — all honoured, none owed a deviation\n   247\t\n   248\t- D3's table implemented row for row, including the non-outcome fold to\n   249\t  `transport-error` with `:dao.stream/answer` retained (a row no test\n   250\t  exercises on a real transport — noted below under left owing).\n   251\t- D6 verbatim, `checked` on mint and every read, incremental flattening,\n   252\t  totality throw kept and now pinned (F4).\n   253\t- D8's seven edits and D10's enumeration followed; the enumeration was\n   254\t  re-derived, not trusted: `publish!` forwarding `{:manifest-address …\n   255\t  :manifest …}` unchanged and `SchemaWrapper.closed?` reading its own flag\n   256\t  were checked against the tree and matched the plan's table; no fifth\n   257\t  forwarding surface exists.\n   258\t- §7's deletions done with the F4 distinction kept: transport fixtures for\n   259\t  excluded outcomes gone, consumer-side doubles proving the precondition\n   260\t  checks added.\n   261\t- §8's four placements written, each naming `memory-log` and carrying the\n   262\t  verbatim sentence that a reader/writer surface check does not establish\n   263\t  retention.\n   264\t\n   265\t## Left owing (none of it Phase 2 scope)\n   266\t\n   267\t- **Phase 3** (§5): the published adapter's `ds/defopen`/`PublishedIndexStream`\n   268\t  deletion, the eleven adapter read paths' migration (including\n   269\t  `stigmergy_test`'s `sources`), `index_test`'s remaining 35 `ds/` sites,\n   270\t  `stream-values` (:122) and the :777 v2-ringbuffer carrier, the P5\n   271\t  close-exactly-once test, and the three Phase-3 doc edits (§5.7).\n   272\t- **Untested branch, inherited not introduced:** D3's non-outcome fold\n   273\t  (`append-packet!` folding a malformed local answer to\n   274\t  `:dao.stream/transport-error` + `:dao.stream/answer`) has no test — no\n   275\t  double in the suite answers a non-map from `append!`. The plan's §4.6\n   276\t  lists no test for it either; adding one would be a one-line double\n   277\t  (`append!` answering `:boom`) if the owner wants the row pinned.\n   278\t- The `bb test:clj`-time suite has no per-test timeout configured; the D6\n   279\t  spin guard is pinned by the no-cursor double, but a future regression\n   280\t  would hang rather than fail (the plan's §10 note, restated for whoever\n   281\t  wires the runner).\n   282\t\n   283\tNothing was staged or committed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
