md:35:Membership is **dynamic**: opening a member log (`ds/open!` through the handle) *is* joining the space; closing it leaves. Every writer owns its **own** log, so writes never contend or need routing — there is no shared write cursor to merge. The space is heterogeneous along two axes: member logs differ in **dimension/type** (one carries only d5, another only d10), and in how strict they are (some enforce their type on write, some accept anything). Reads range over all member logs at once; an **interpreter** is the read-side projection that folds those logs into a queryable view — its materialization of a stream is a **slice**: the stream quotiented by an interpreter-defined equivalence relation.\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:61:member logs (`1..n`, each opened by `ds/open!` through the handle, joining and\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:88:handle (`(ds/open! {:type :dao-stream :space space ...})`) and append with that\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:89:stream's own `put!`. Each `ds/open!` returns a **distinct** `dao.stream.file` with\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:99:(`dao.stream.file`, opened via `ds/open!`) carry datoms **in**; the space answers\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:107:      log   (ds/open! {:type :dao-stream :space space})] ; my own member write log\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:154:            ds/open! {:space …}    │            │  dao.space/q   (Datalog)\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:199:  `ds/open!` into a live transport.\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:205:  (ds/open! (resource->descriptor (read-resource space stream-eid)))\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:259:(def ledger (ds/open! {:type :dao-stream :space space :name \"ledger\"\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:263:(def ingest (ds/open! {:type :dao-stream :space space :name \"ingest\"\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:516:  (let [log (ds/open! {:type :dao-stream :space space :name \"producer\"})]\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:525:  (let [log (ds/open! {:type :dao-stream :space space :name worker-id})]\ndocs/design/dao.sp