{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '260,420p' collab/1788953799216-storage-space-transactor-phase2.glm-5.3.findings.md\nnl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc | sed -n '130,280p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc | sed -n '435,505p'\nrg -n \\\"#\\\\?\\\\(:clj\\\" src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc src/cljc/dao/space/schema.cljc test/dao/space/{transactor,index,query,schema}_test.cljc test/dao/space/stigmergy_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"  checks added.\n- §8's four placements written, each naming `memory-log` and carrying the\n  verbatim sentence that a reader/writer surface check does not establish\n  retention.\n\n## Left owing (none of it Phase 2 scope)\n\n- **Phase 3** (§5): the published adapter's `ds/defopen`/`PublishedIndexStream`\n  deletion, the eleven adapter read paths' migration (including\n  `stigmergy_test`'s `sources`), `index_test`'s remaining 35 `ds/` sites,\n  `stream-values` (:122) and the :777 v2-ringbuffer carrier, the P5\n  close-exactly-once test, and the three Phase-3 doc edits (§5.7).\n- **Untested branch, inherited not introduced:** D3's non-outcome fold\n  (`append-packet!` folding a malformed local answer to\n  `:dao.stream/transport-error` + `:dao.stream/answer`) has no test — no\n  double in the suite answers a non-map from `append!`. The plan's §4.6\n  lists no test for it either; adding one would be a one-line double\n  (`append!` answering `:boom`) if the owner wants the row pinned.\n- The `bb test:clj`-time suite has no per-test timeout configured; the D6\n  spin guard is pinned by the no-cursor double, but a future regression\n  would hang rather than fail (the plan's §10 note, restated for whoever\n  wires the runner).\n\nNothing was staged or committed.\n   130\t            {:history datoms})))\n   131\t      (inc (reduce max ts)))))\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn- append-packet!\n   135\t  \"Append one atomic transaction record to the local stream. The answer is\n   136\t   validated with the contract's own validator before it is interpreted:\n   137\t   :dao.stream/ok advances the watermark and returns the v2 receipt; any\n   138\t   other conforming outcome is returned as data with the watermark\n   139\t   unchanged, so the same t is still pending and retrying the identical\n   140\t   call re-attempts it; a non-outcome answer is folded to\n   141\t   :dao.stream/transport-error with the raw answer retained under\n   142\t   :dao.stream/answer.\"\n   143\t  [local-stream next-t t datoms]\n   144\t  (let [record {:dao.space/transaction {:t t, :datoms datoms}}\n   145\t        answer (stream/append! local-stream record)]\n   146\t    (if-not (stream/valid-outcome? :append! answer)\n   147\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   148\t       :dao.stream/answer answer}\n   149\t      (do (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   150\t            (swap! next-t inc))\n   151\t          (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   152\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   153\t             :dao.space/t t\n   154\t             :dao.space/datoms datoms}\n   155\t            answer)))))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(defn create!\n   159\t  \"Create a transactor value from a spec — the value, or a throw: the\n   160\t   failure modes are a malformed spec and a malformed retained history,\n   161\t   both of which a caller can only abort on.\n   162\t\n   163\t   Validates surfaces, never retention (D2/T18): stream/reader? and\n   164\t   stream/writer? check the dao.stream reader and writer surfaces, and\n   165\t   neither establishes the complete-retention transport the history scan\n   166\t   requires. The host composition supplies a handle created by\n   167\t   dao.stream.memory-log/create!; supplying an evicting transport is a\n   168\t   host-assembly defect — detectable, deliberately not checked, because a\n   169\t   type check would couple dao.space to memory-log by name and reject a\n   170\t   future correct complete-retention transport.\"\n   171\t  [spec]\n   172\t  (let [{:keys [local-stream intake-pool name]} spec]\n   173\t    (when (contains? spec :next-t)\n   174\t      (throw\n   175\t        (ex-info\n   176\t          \"the transactor derives transaction time from retained history; :next-t is not accepted\"\n   177\t          {:spec spec})))\n   178\t    (when-not (and (stream/reader? local-stream)\n   179\t                   (stream/writer? local-stream))\n   180\t      (throw\n   181\t        (ex-info\n   182\t          \"transactor spec requires a :local-stream satisfying the dao.stream reader and writer surfaces\"\n   183\t          {:spec spec})))\n   184\t    (when-not (and (coll? intake-pool) (seq intake-pool))\n   185\t      (throw\n   186\t        (ex-info\n   187\t          \"transactor spec requires a non-empty :intake-pool of streams satisfying the dao.stream writer surface\"\n   188\t          {:spec spec})))\n   189\t    (doseq [intake intake-pool]\n   190\t      (when-not (stream/writer? intake)\n   191\t        (throw\n   192\t          (ex-info\n   193\t            \"transactor :intake-pool members must satisfy IDaoStreamWriter\"\n   194\t            {:intake-pool intake-pool}))))\n   195\t    (let [t (derive-next-t (index/snapshot-datoms local-stream))]\n   196\t      {:dao.space/transactor true\n   197\t       :local-stream local-stream\n   198\t       :intake-pool intake-pool\n   199\t       :name (or name \"transactor\")\n   200\t       :next-t (atom t)\n   201\t       :state (atom {:closed false})})))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t(defn append!\n   205\t  \"Append one entity map or datom vector as a single atomic transaction.\n   206\t   Answers the v2 receipt on ok — {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   207\t   :dao.space/t t :dao.space/datoms datoms} — the local append's conforming\n   208\t   outcome as data otherwise (watermark unchanged, same t still pending),\n   209\t   and {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed} on a closed transactor.\n   210\t   A malformed value still throws: it is a defect in the caller's own\n   211\t   argument, detected before any stream is touched.\"\n   212\t  [log val]\n   213\t  (let [{:keys [local-stream next-t state]} log]\n   214\t    (with-write-lock\n   215\t      next-t\n   216\t      (fn []\n   217\t        (if (:closed @state)\n   218\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}\n   219\t          (let [t @next-t\n   220\t                datoms (val->datoms val t)]\n   221\t            (when (empty? datoms)\n   222\t              (throw (ex-info \"append! produced no datoms\" {:val val})))\n   223\t            (append-packet! local-stream next-t t datoms)))))))\n   224\t\n   225\t\n   226\t(defn transact!\n   227\t  \"Commits a non-empty collection of entity maps or datom vectors as a\n   228\t  single atomic transaction: every datom shares one allocated t and lands\n   229\t  in one transaction record through exactly one local append, so no partial\n   230\t  prefix is possible. Answers the v2 receipt on ok, the local append's\n   231\t  conforming outcome as data otherwise, and\n   232\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed} on a closed transactor. Throws\n   233\t  when the collection is empty, any item is invalid, or the expansion\n   234\t  yields no datoms.\"\n   235\t  [log tx-data]\n   236\t  (when (empty? tx-data)\n   237\t    (throw (ex-info \"transact! requires at least one transaction item\"\n   238\t                    {:tx-data tx-data})))\n   239\t  (let [{:keys [local-stream next-t state]} log]\n   240\t    (with-write-lock\n   241\t      next-t\n   242\t      (fn []\n   243\t        (if (:closed @state)\n   244\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}\n   245\t          (let [t @next-t\n   246\t                datoms (into [] (mapcat #(val->datoms % t)) tx-data)]\n   247\t            (when (empty? datoms)\n   248\t              (throw (ex-info \"transact! produced no datoms\" {:tx-data tx-data})))\n   249\t            (append-packet! local-stream next-t t datoms)))))))\n   250\t\n   251\t\n   252\t(defn close!\n   253\t  \"Close this transactor value: further append!/transact! answer\n   254\t   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed} rather than throwing. Per\n   255\t   value — neither the local stream nor the intake pool is closed or\n   256\t   erased. Idempotent; linearizes after an in-flight append.\"\n   257\t  [log]\n   258\t  (let [{:keys [next-t state]} log]\n   259\t    (with-write-lock\n   260\t      next-t\n   261\t      (fn []\n   262\t        (swap! state assoc :closed true)\n   263\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn publish!\n   267\t  \"Build and enqueue the covered indexes over the local stream into the\n   268\t   intake pool (dao.space.index/publish-index!), returning its\n   269\t   {:manifest-address ... :manifest ...}. opts are passed through to\n   270\t   publish-index! (e.g. :branching-factor, :select-stream). Publication is\n   271\t   explicit and acknowledges enqueuing only, never observer\n   272\t   materialization.\"\n   273\t  ([log] (publish! log nil))\n   274\t  ([log opts]\n   275\t   (index/publish-index! (:local-stream log) (:intake-pool log) opts)))\n   435\t      :else\n   436\t      (throw\n   437\t        (ex-info\n   438\t          \"local stream payload must be a datom or dao.space transaction record\"\n   439\t          {:payload payload})))))\n   440\t\n   441\t\n   442\t(defn datoms-from-elements\n   443\t  \"Flatten a seq of local-stream elements to canonical local d5 datoms —\n   444\t   the payload vocabulary's public, seq-level spelling. Each element is\n   445\t   validated and flattened by the same per-element rule snapshot-datoms\n   446\t   applies inside its read loop: a canonical datom vector passes through, an\n   447\t   atomic {:dao.space/transaction {:t n :datoms [...]}} record flattens to\n   448\t   its datoms, and anything malformed throws.\"\n   449\t  [elements]\n   450\t  (into [] (mapcat element-datoms) elements))\n   451\t\n   452\t\n   453\t(defn- checked\n   454\t  \"Fold a defective result into an exception before anything is read from it.\n   455\t   The contract's own validator (dao.stream/validate-outcome) answers nil\n   456\t   for a conforming result and a defect map otherwise; interpreting an\n   457\t   unvalidated result is how a loop ends up recurring on a nil cursor.\"\n   458\t  [operation result]\n   459\t  (if-let [defect (stream/validate-outcome operation result)]\n   460\t    (throw (ex-info \"malformed local stream result\"\n   461\t                    {:operation operation, :result result, :defect defect}))\n   462\t    result))\n   463\t\n   464\t\n   465\t(defn snapshot-datoms\n   466\t  \"Read an agent-local stream in full and flatten it to canonical local d5\n   467\t   datoms.\n   468\t\n   469\t   The local stream is on a complete-retention transport\n   470\t   (dao.stream.memory-log), so a fresh :oldest cursor is the origin and\n   471\t   `gap` cannot occur — completeness comes from the transport's declared\n   472\t   retention, never from the anchor (dao.stream.md, *Complete history*).\n   473\t   `blocked` (an open stream caught up) and `end` (a closed one fully read)\n   474\t   finish the read at the tail. Each element is validated and flattened as it\n   475\t   is read, so the first defect in stream order is the one reported and no\n   476\t   read happens past it. A well-formed but unexpected outcome means the handle\n   477\t   is not the transport the composition owes.\"\n   478\t  [local-stream]\n   479\t  (let [mint (checked :cursor (stream/cursor local-stream :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   480\t    (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome mint))\n   481\t      (throw (ex-info \"local stream refused an :oldest cursor\" {:result mint})))\n   482\t    (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor mint)\n   483\t           datoms []]\n   484\t      (let [r (checked :next (stream/next local-stream cursor))]\n   485\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   486\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   487\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r)\n   488\t                 (into datoms (element-datoms (:dao.stream/value r))))\n   489\t          (:dao.stream/blocked :dao.stream/end) datoms\n   490\t          (throw (ex-info \"local stream is not a complete-retention transport\"\n   491\t                          {:outcome (:dao.stream/outcome r), :result r})))))))\n   492\t\n   493\t\n   494\t(defn- recording-content-handle\n   495\t  \"Temporary in-memory content store for the publish build. :put-content-fn\n   496\t   records each unique node blob on first insertion (answering :present for\n   497\t   duplicates, so the recorded order is first-insertion order, deduplicated);\n   498\t   :get-content-fn reads recorded blobs back. Addresses are minted by\n   499\t   jing/materialize! through dao.data.btree.storage/kv-storage, so the\n   500\t   recorded order is exactly the store-tree children-before-parent traversal.\n   501\t   The handle is a build-time value: no global state is introduced.\"\n   502\t  []\n   503\t  (let [state (atom {:content {}, :order []})]\n   504\t    {:state state,\n   505\t     :put-content-fn (fn [address payload]\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:22:  #?(:cljs (:require-macros [dao.stream])))\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:192:          #?(:cljs js/Error\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:238:          #?(:cljs js/Error\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:564:            #?(:cljs js/Error\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:571:            #?(:cljs js/Error\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:584:              #?(:cljs js/Error\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:640:          #?(:cljs js/Error\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:680:  #?(:clj @(.-state ^dao.space.schema.SchemaWrapper w)\ntest/dao/space/schema_test.cljc:770:            #?(:cljs js/Err